  un-skippable
        [ oracle.sh:2:1
     2 | eval "one"
       | \__/
  error[syntax-unsupported]: sm `eval` executes constructed code (un-analyzable)
        [ oracle.sh:2:1
     2 | eval "one"
       | \__/
  2:1 info [unmodeled-inventory:unmodeled-wall-inventory] sm 2 unmodeled ⊤-walls in this book; the first is here. Downstream commands (~3 leaf site(s) after it) lose full-elision and fall back to runtime guards until each wall's tool has an oracle.
  error[cfg-top-node]: sm unsupported construct (unknown): un-probeable and
  un-skippable
        [ oracle.sh:3:1
     3 | eval "two"
       | \__/
  error[syntax-unsupported]: sm `eval` executes constructed code (un-analyzable)
        [ oracle.sh:3:1
     3 | eval "two"
       | \__/

